# ta_prefill_knee.yaml.in
#
# SHORT-OUTPUT / PREFILL-DOMINATED profile -- ~2000 in / ~100 out.
# The autoscaling-viz cross-check's item 5 (session-notes/status/benchmark.md
# §17.11), carried as its own run rather than as a leg of ta_autoscale_dwell.
#
# WHY IT IS A SEPARATE RUN, NOT A LEG
#
# It moves the STIMULUS. ta_autoscale_dwell.yaml.in moves the rate ladder while
# holding the token shape fixed at 2048/512, which is what keeps it comparable to
# the 08-07 ladder and staircase. Appending a 100-out leg to it would move shape
# and rate together and leave no clean axis back to either. It also does not fit:
# both profiles are sized against the same 20Gi results PVC, and each needs the
# PVC reclaimed before it runs.
#
# THE ARITHMETIC THAT MAKES THIS PROFILE NECESSARY
#
# Our existing "prefill heavy" shapes are not prefill-heavy in any useful sense.
# On the 08-07 arm A run at 2048 in / 512 out: TTFT mean 0.192 s, TPOT mean
# 0.0217 s => decode ~= 512 x 0.0217 = 11.1 s against ~0.19 s of prefill. Decode
# is ~98% of request time. 4K-in/1K-out is WORSE, not better -- lengthening the
# input while lengthening the output keeps decode dominant. Prefill dominance
# needs SHORT OUTPUTS, which is what this profile is.
#
# At 100 out the same numbers give ~2.17 s decode + ~0.19 s prefill ~= 2.36 s, so
# ~4.7x faster per request => the single-replica wall moves from the observed
# ~6 rps to roughly ~28 rps. The rate ladder below is scaled to that, which is
# also why its cluster footprint is SMALLER than the dwell profile's despite the
# higher rates (see Footprint).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: the ITL LOWER KNEE. On 08-07, below saturation `itl ~ running`
# alone already reaches r^2 0.93-0.94 and adding a prefill term buys +0.001;
# in-band (kv ~0.99) the same term buys +0.236. Prefill is a regime-specific
# term, so a shape that isolates it is worth having. Note the confound that
# motivated this: on that run corr(prefill/s, prompt/s) = +0.96, so the apparent
# corr(itl, prefill/s) = +0.78 cannot be attributed. Holding output length short
# and sweeping rate is how the two are separated.
#
# CAVEAT -- SAME OPERATING-POINT PROBLEM AS THE DWELL PROFILE, stated so it is not
# discovered mid-analysis. A knee is a property of load per replica, and the
# autoscaler's job is precisely to keep load per replica off the knee. Sweeping
# offered rate under an active controller therefore samples whatever operating
# point the controller holds, not the curve. Per-stage ITL against MEASURED
# concurrency-per-replica is still a valid point on the curve at each rung, so
# this run is not wasted -- but the sharp instrument for a knee is a FIXED replica
# count with autoscaling off, which is an analyzer/scenario change and so is the
# planner's and Dean's call. Raised in
# plans/session/handoffs/plan__benchmark-next-run-capture-list.md.
#
# SIZING -- and this is an ESTIMATE with a stated model, unlike the dwell profile
# whose 535 KB/req is measured at its own token shape.
#   Measured: 4,234,888,579 B / 7920 req = 535 KB/req at 2048 in / 512 out.
#   That cannot be input-dominated: 2048 tokens of prompt text is ~8-10 KB, three
#   orders off. 535 KB / 512 output tokens ~= 1.05 KB per OUTPUT token, which is
#   consistent with a verbose per-output-token record. So the defensible model is
#   output-proportional, giving ~100 x 1.05 KB + ~20 KB fixed ~= 125 KB/req here.
#
#   requests = 180x10 + 180x25 + 180x45 + 480x5
#            = 1800 + 4500 + 8100 + 2400 = 16,800
#   expected ~= 16,800 x 125 KB  ~= 2.1 GB
#   worst case (if the model is wrong and size is shape-independent at 535 KB/req)
#            ~= 16,800 x 535 KB  ~= 9.0 GB
# The rung count is set by the WORST case, not the expected one: 9.0 GB still fits
# a reclaimed 20Gi PVC with margin. If the run confirms ~2 GB, a follow-up can
# afford 4-5x more rungs and should take them -- three load rungs is thin for a
# curve fit and is a budget compromise, not a design preference.
# Wall clock: 180+180+180+480 = 1,020 s ~= 17 min of load.
#
# FOOTPRINT: at a ~28 rps/replica wall, 45 rps implies ~1.6 => 2 decode replicas.
# This is the CHEAPER of the two profiles on a shared cluster despite the higher
# offered rates. maxReplicas 10 will not bind.
load:
  type: constant
  # Same seed as the ladder/dwell profiles. Note the output distribution differs,
  # so sampled output lengths are NOT the ladder's -- only this profile repeats.
  base_seed: 42
  stages:
  - rate: 10
    duration: 180
  - rate: 25
    duration: 180
  - rate: 45
    duration: 180
  # Descent: keeps the scale-down path and the 0.70 watermark in-window, and is
  # the ">=300 s after load stops" window (480 s). Trickle rather than zero for
  # the same reason as the dwell profile -- no requests means nothing observes the
  # drain.
  - rate: 5
    duration: 480
api:
  type: completion
  streaming: true
server:
  type: vllm
  model_name: REPLACE_ENV_LLMDBENCH_DEPLOY_CURRENT_MODEL
  base_url: REPLACE_ENV_LLMDBENCH_HARNESS_STACK_ENDPOINT_URL
  ignore_eos: true
tokenizer:
  pretrained_model_name_or_path: REPLACE_ENV_LLMDBENCH_DEPLOY_CURRENT_MODEL
data:
  type: random
  # Input held at the ladder's shape so input is the CONTROLLED variable and only
  # output length moves.
  input_distribution:
    min: 2000
    max: 2100
    mean: 2048
    std_dev: 40
    total_count: 2000
  # The change. std_dev scaled with the mean (512 -> 100 is ~5x, 20 -> 4) so the
  # coefficient of variation matches the ladder and dispersion is not a second
  # moving variable.
  output_distribution:
    min: 90
    max: 110
    mean: 100
    std_dev: 4
    total_count: 2000
report:
  request_lifecycle:
    summary: true
    per_stage: true
    # DELIBERATE EXCEPTION to per_request being disabled elsewhere (staircase,
    # ladder, dwell, calibration probe): per-request ITL IS the measurement here,
    # and the gateway access log cannot substitute (no TTFT, no per-token
    # timing). Safe to keep because this run is short and comfortably sized --
    # ~17 min wall clock, worst-case ~9.0 GB (see SIZING above) against a
    # reclaimed 20Gi PVC, unlike the dwell profile's 11.3 GB collector that OOM'd
    # against an ~11.9 GB harness pod boundary. If this profile's shape or
    # duration changes, re-check the sizing math before assuming this still fits.
    per_request: true
storage:
  local_storage:
    path: /workspace
